   look mismatched.

   We also apply the dark-mode value via prefers-color-scheme in
   addition to html.dark. Mintlify renders the SSR HTML without
   .dark on <html> and only adds it after hydration; meanwhile
   the page background already paints dark (inlined from
   docs.json background.color.dark). That gap is what causes the
   "flash" where pills look like light-mode washes on a dark
   page. prefers-color-scheme lands the right color on first paint
   for the common case (system-dark users); html.dark re-asserts
   it for users who manually toggle dark on a light system.

   Values are subtle neutral washes — visible enough to read as
   pill chrome on either surface, quiet enough not to compete with
   the search bar and the primary CTA.

   Trade-off: a user with a dark system preference who has
   manually toggled the docs to light will briefly see a
   transparent-looking pill on a white page, because the @media
   rule wins until hydration adds .dark (or in this case, removes
   the absence-of-.dark default) and the page repaints. Acceptable
   until we add a pre-paint inline script that reads localStorage
   and sets the theme class before first paint.
